div><p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/nyc/">New York</a> / Hanging signs that use the overhead space</p><p class="eyebrow">VISION GRAPHICS · NEW YORK</p><h1>Hanging signs that use the overhead space</h1><p class="lead">Hanging signs can make a destination visible when wall space is limited or when a message needs to be seen above surrounding activity. An interior department sign, a suspended reception marker and an exterior hanging identity are different projects with different support requirements. Vision Graphics can help New York businesses develop the artwork and format around the actual viewing direction. Start with the available overhead area, the message and the site’s restrictions, then review the supporting structure and placement before choosing a production approach.</p><p class="review-note">Planning guide · </p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn primary" href="/nyc/contact/?product=Hanging%20signs%20that%20use%20the%20overhead%20space">Discuss your project <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="17" height="17" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="#options">Explore options <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></div><figure class="project-image product-photo"><img src="/nyc/assets/mcs-new-service-exterior-signs-960.webp" srcset="/nyc/assets/mcs-new-service-exterior-signs-480.webp 480w, /nyc/assets/mcs-new-service-exterior-signs-960.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 50vw" alt="Signage example related to Hanging signs that use the overhead space" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Illustrative sign example · Michigan Custom Signs source</figcaption></figure></section><section class="wrap section article-layout"><article><section><h2>Design for the angle of approach</h2><p>Determine whether the sign needs one readable face or two. Keep the message short enough to recognize while moving, and consider what sits behind the sign from each direction. A strong silhouette and clear contrast may be more useful than fine detail.</p></section><section><h2>Treat suspension as part of the project</h2><p>Document ceiling or bracket conditions, clearances, access and any restrictions from the property team. The support system must be appropriate for the sign and location. Exterior exposure adds further considerations, so interior and exterior concepts should not share an assumed mounting specification.</p></section><section id="options"><p class="eyebrow">MATERIALS &amp; APPROACHES</p><h2>Find the right fit.</h2><div class="options-grid"><div><h3>Interior department markers</h3><p>Identify aisles, service areas or destinations from a distance.</p></div><div><h3>Double-sided panels</h3><p>Present the message to people approaching from opposite directions.</p></div><div><h3>Branded hanging identities</h3><p>Explore a shaped or rectangular panel that fits the surrounding architecture.</p></div></div></section><section><h2>Where it can work</h2><ul class="check-list"><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Retail departments</li><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Event and exhibition areas</li><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Reviewed exterior entrances</li></ul></section><section class="faqs"><h2>A few useful answers.</h2><details><summary>Can a hanging sign be double-sided?<span>+</span></summary><p>Yes, the layout can account for two approaches. Placement and support details still need review for the chosen format.</p></details><details><summary>Can any ceiling support a sign?<span>+</span></summary><p>No. The supporting structure and fixing method must be assessed for the site and sign.</p></details></section></article><aside class="product-aside"><p class="eyebrow">LET’S START WITH THE DETAILS</p><h3>Have a space in mind?</h3><p>A photo, a few measurements and your project ZIP help us ask the right questions.</p><a href="/nyc/contact/?photo=1" class="btn dark"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="17" height="17" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-camera" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13.997 4a2 2 0 0 1 1.76 1.05l.486.9A2 2 0 0 0 18.003 7H20a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V9a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h1.997a2 2 0 0 0 1.759-1.048l.489-.904A2 2 0 0 1 10.004 4z"></path><circle cx="12" cy="13" r="3"></circle></svg> Send a project photo</a><hr><h3>Related possibilities</h3><a href="/nyc/blade-signs/">Blade signs<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="15" height="15" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><a href="/nyc/directional-signs/">Directional signs<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000